{
  "configuration_id": "config_004",
  "reason": "Evidence: We have only two completed experiments, both RNA-only single-profile. scvi_n200 (config_008, acc=0.520) outperforms pca_n2000 (config_002, acc=0.485), establishing scvi_n200 as the stronger RNA encoder. However, we have zero information on whether the image modality contributes any predictive value. Question: config_004 (multimodal, singleprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, concat) directly tests whether adding a standard image encoder with simple concatenation fusion improves over the best RNA-only baseline (config_008), while keeping the RNA encoder and profile setting identical to isolate the image contribution. Why best: This is the single most critical design decision for a multimodal study—if image adds no value, the entire search space collapses to RNA-only variants. Using the simplest fusion (concat) and a standard encoder (resnet50) avoids confounding the image-contribution question with fusion complexity or encoder capacity. A positive result justifies further exploration of fusion/aggregation; a null result redirects budget to RNA-only multiprofile or encoder comparisons."
}

